cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "STANet: controlled evaluation of hybrid LSTM-GAT architectures for traffic anomaly detection"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for a controlled, multi-seed evaluation of the design
  choices underlying a hybrid LSTM + Graph Attention Network traffic anomaly
  detector. Contains the full experiment pipeline (encoder benchmark, fusion
  ablation, graph-construction ablation, trip-grouped cross-validation,
  trip-level cluster statistics, efficiency measurements), the synthetic
  trajectory dataset generated over an OpenStreetMap-derived road network,
  and every result file reported in the paper.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/keremkartal/Anomaly-Detection"
keywords:
  - traffic anomaly detection
  - graph attention network
  - long short-term memory
  - multimodal fusion
  - ablation study
  - evaluation methodology
  - reproducibility
